\Section{Two distinct management responses}
\textbf{Build-skill acquisition.} Its more durable economics make this a candidate for acquisition investment with a cash-payback constraint. The favorable partner cell does not establish that increasing partner spend will produce the same customers at the same CAC.

\textbf{Save-time experience.} Investigate whether a shorter use cycle reflects successful task completion, limited recurring need or an experience problem. The current event and survey flags do not distinguish those explanations. Measure the proposition and onboarding experience, then track renewal and contribution at matched customer ages.
