The operational review should track whether renewal and contribution continue to improve at the same customer ages. The acquisition review should track whether channel iCAC changes with spending and whether newly acquired customers resemble the value benchmark. A lower reported CAC alone is insufficient when a channel mainly captures people who would have acquired without its campaign.
\Boundary{The channel tests support decisions at their tested spending levels and eligible audiences. Repeat acquisition holdouts when these change. Keep forecast risk and cash-payback capacity visible when applying the value estimates.}

